{
  "title": "Trapping Rain Water",
  "difficulty": "hard",
  "args": [
    "integer[]"
  ],
  "returnType": "integer",
  "constraints": [
    "n == height.length",
    "1 <= n <= 2 * 10^4",
    "0 <= height[i] <= 10^5"
  ],
  "description": "Given `n` non-negative integers representing an elevation map where the width of each bar is `1`, compute how much water it can **trap** after raining.\n\n```text\n                #\n    #       # # # # # #\n  # # #   # # # # # # #\n  0 1 0 2 1 0 1 3 2 1 2 1\n    ~   ~   ~ ~   ~ ~ ~ ~   <- ~ marks trapped water\n```\n\nFor `height = [0,1,0,2,1,0,1,3,2,1,2,1]`, the total trapped water = **6**.",
  "tests": [
    {
      "input": "[0,1,0,2,1,0,1,3,2,1,2,1]",
      "expected": "6",
      "explanation": "The elevation map traps 6 units of rain water total.",
      "is_single_array_arg": true,
      "isSample": true
    },
    {
      "input": "[4,2,0,3,2,5]",
      "expected": "9",
      "explanation": "Water fills the valleys: positions 1,2,3,4 trap 2+4+1+2=9 units.",
      "is_single_array_arg": true,
      "isSample": true
    },
    {
      "input": "[3,0,3]",
      "expected": "3",
      "is_single_array_arg": true,
      "isSample": true
    },
    {
      "input": "[1]",
      "expected": "0",
      "is_single_array_arg": true,
      "isSample": false
    },
    {
      "input": "[1,2]",
      "expected": "0",
      "is_single_array_arg": true,
      "isSample": false
    },
    {
      "input": "[3,3,3,3]",
      "expected": "0",
      "is_single_array_arg": true,
      "isSample": false
    },
    {
      "input": "[0,0,0,0]",
      "expected": "0",
      "is_single_array_arg": true,
      "isSample": false
    },
    {
      "input": "[5,0,0,0,5]",
      "expected": "15",
      "is_single_array_arg": true,
      "isSample": false
    },
    {
      "input": "[1,7,2,3,4,5,6,1]",
      "expected": "10",
      "is_single_array_arg": true,
      "isSample": false
    },
    {
      "input": "[2,0,2]",
      "expected": "2",
      "is_single_array_arg": true,
      "isSample": false
    }
  ]
}
